// Regression test: a struct method declaration referencing a misspelled
// struct name must still be rejected, even though ParseFuncDef() now builds
// `self`'s type lazily (as a NamedType placeholder) instead of eagerly
// resolving it via GlobalSymbolTable -- a change that was necessary to
// support declaring a method before its struct (see
// 19_method_before_struct.tr), but which also meant the old eager
// "Unknown struct type 'X' in method declaration" parse-time check no
// longer fires for a genuine typo. Resolver.cpp's validateNamedType(),
// applied to every parameter (including the implicit `self`) in
// visitFuncDef(), is where this validation now correctly lives instead.

struct User {
    age: int
}

fn Usre.grow(): void {
    self.age = self.age + 1;
}

fn main(): int {
    return 0;
}
